    "narrative": "Our core offensive output today hinges on the duo of **Kyle Tucker** (73.73) and **Andy Pages** (68.03), who represent our strongest plays against Gallen. While Gallen poses a legitimate challenge, both players carry high base projections and benefit from positive park factors and favorable lineup placement, with **Kyle Tucker** in particular offering the safest floor due to his consistent production profile. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.39) rounds out our elite tier; despite a slight hit from the dynamic platoon split against the right-handed Holmes, his high xwOBA and the prime #3 spot in the order keep him locked as an anchor for the lineup.\n\nThe marginal decisions at the bottom of the order reflect our aggressive pursuit of efficiency over pure raw projection. **Sam Antonacci** (54.77) earns the start over **Miguel Vargas** (51.38) largely due to the massive boost provided by the leadoff spot; while **Miguel Vargas** remains a solid contributor, the projected run-scoring opportunities for **Sam Antonacci** against Bradley tipped the scales in his favor. Conversely, **Jackson Merrill** (38.94) was relegated to the bench as he fell below our 40-point efficiency floor, heavily penalized by a difficult matchup against the lefty S\u00e1nchez and a suboptimal #7 batting order slot.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus today given the volatility of the opposing rotation. We are navigating a tough assignment for **Miguel Andujar** (51.81) and **Coby Mayo** (52.06) as they face the high-end talent of S\u00e1nchez and Tolle, respectively. While **Gunnar Henderson** (53.96) is naturally in the lineup, his score is suppressed today by the dynamic platoon disadvantage against the lefty Tolle. We will monitor the weather reports for these contests, but as it stands, our composition is optimized to maximize the scarcity of stolen bases and run production across the board.",
